  "question": {
    "text": "The limiting molar conductivities $\\Lambda^{\\circ}$ for $\\mathrm{NaCl}, \\mathrm{KBr}$ and $\\mathrm{KCl}$ are 126,152 and $150 \\mathrm{~S} \\mathrm{~cm}^2 \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively. The $\\Lambda^{\\circ}$ for $\\mathrm{NaBr}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$128 \\mathrm{~S} \\mathrm{~cm}^2 \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$302 \\mathrm{~S} \\mathrm{~cm}^2 \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$278 \\mathrm{~S} \\mathrm{~cm}^2 \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$176 \\mathrm{~S} \\mathrm{~cm}^2 \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{NaCl}}^{\\circ}=\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Na}}^{\\circ}+\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Cl}}^{\\circ}=126 \\ldots(1)$\n$\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{KBr}}^{\\circ}=\\lambda_{\\mathrm{K}^{+}}^{\\circ}+\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Br}^{-}}^{\\circ}=152$\n$\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{KCl}}^{\\circ}=\\lambda_{\\mathrm{K}^{+}}^{\\circ}+\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}}^{\\circ}=150$\n$\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{NaBr}}^{\\circ}=\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Na}}^{\\circ}+\\lambda_{\\mathrm{Br}^{-}}^{\\circ}$\n$\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{NaBr}}^{\\circ}=126+152-150=128$"
  }
}